From f453428828716a1cca443b623d2503a47693a53a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "T. Kurt Bond" <tkurtbond@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:16:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 67/67] ethReals: set H and L, the offsets of a LONGREAL's two
 halves

ExpoL, SetExpoL, RealL and IntL read and write a LONGREAL's high and
low 32 bits at the offsets H and L, which the comment says to set for
the machine's byte order, and which the module used to set with a
dynamic test ("7.11.1995 jt: dynamic endianess test"). Nothing sets them
now, so both are 0, and on a little-endian machine every one of these
procedures uses the low half for the high one: ethReals.ExpoL(12345.678D0)
is 1163, not 1036. ethReals.Ten uses ExpoL and SetExpoL, and
ethStrings.RealToStr and RealToFixStr use ExpoL, so
ethStrings.RealToStr(12345.678D0, s) gave "0.000000000000005D+042", and
RealToStr of 0.25 and of 3.0 gave "0".

The module body now sets H and L from Platform.LittleEndian.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/library/s3/ethReals.Mod | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/library/s3/ethReals.Mod b/src/library/s3/ethReals.Mod
index 484b186c..6a388852 100644
--- a/src/library/s3/ethReals.Mod
+++ b/src/library/s3/ethReals.Mod
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
 Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Z…rich.
 *)
 
-IMPORT SYSTEM, Modules;
+IMPORT SYSTEM, Modules, Platform;
 
 (* Bernd Moesli
   Seminar for Applied Mathematics
@@ -224,6 +224,8 @@
 END RealX;
 
 BEGIN
+  (* the offsets of the high and low 32 bits of a LONGREAL *)
+  IF Platform.LittleEndian THEN H := 4; L := 0 ELSE H := 0; L := 4 END;
   RealX(03FF0000000000000H, tene[0]);
   RealX(04024000000000000H, tene[1]);    (*  1 *)
   RealX(04059000000000000H, tene[2]);    (*  2 *)
-- 
